<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Armand Bouchart</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">12th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Armand Bouchart was a Knight Templar who governed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyprus">Cyprus</a> for the order after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/knights-templar">Templars</a> bought the island from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/richard-i-of-england">Richard I of England</a> in 1191. His small garrison imposed heavy taxes, provoking a rising in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicosia">Nicosia</a> in April 1192. The Templars returned the island to Richard, who sold it to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guy-of-lusignan">Guy of Lusignan</a>.</p></div>
